{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "The int53 validity guard in front of a proven raw int[] store must use the 64-bit GE/LE comparisons. MIR's `S` suffix selects the 32-bit form, which truncates the int53 bounds to 1 and -1 and makes the guard unsatisfiable, so every proven store falls through to lambda_array_set_checked_inplace_lane. Tune27 T27-9: the int53 band test is one shared 64-bit `add v, INT53_MAX` / `ule t, 2 * INT53_MAX` pair instead of GE/LE/AND. A branch-only guard uses the fused 64-bit UBGT; neither form may be the truncating ULES/UBGTS.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_tune17b_swap_#",
      "expect": [
        "add\t{{r}}, {{r}}, 9007199254740991",
        "{{r}}, 18014398509481982"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        "ules\t{{r}}, {{r}}, 18014398509481982",
        "ubgts\t"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
